  "correctValue": null,
  "solution": {
    "text": "<p>Given condition is,&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>p</mi><mo>&#8743;</mo><mi>q</mi><mo>&#8594;</mo><mfenced><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo>&#8744;</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow></mfenced><mo>&#8743;</mo><mfenced><mrow><mfenced><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>&#8743;</mo><mi>r</mi></mrow></mfenced><mo>&#8594;</mo><mi>q</mi><mo>)</mo></mrow></mfenced><mo>.</mo><mo>.</mo><mo>.</mo><mo>.</mo><mo>.</mo><mo>(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>)</mo></math></p><p>We know conditional disjunction as,</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>p</mi><mo>&#8594;</mo><mi>q</mi><mo>&#8801;</mo><mo>~</mo><mi>p</mi><mo>&#8744;</mo><mi>q</mi></math></p><p>Hence, <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfenced><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>&#8743;</mo><mi>r</mi></mrow></mfenced><mo>&#8594;</mo><mi>q</mi><mo>&#8801;</mo><mo>~</mo><mfenced><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>&#8743;</mo><mi>r</mi></mrow></mfenced><mo>&#8744;</mo><mi>q</mi></math></p><p>Using De Morgan&#39;s law</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfenced><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>&#8743;</mo><mi>r</mi></mrow></mfenced><mo>&#8594;</mo><mi>q</mi><mo>&#8801;</mo><mo>~</mo><mfenced><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>&#8743;</mo><mi>r</mi></mrow></mfenced><mo>&#8744;</mo><mi>q</mi><mo>&#8801;</mo><mfenced><mrow><mo>~</mo><mi>p</mi><mo>&#8744;</mo><mo>~</mo><mi>r</mi></mrow></mfenced><mo>&#8744;</mo><mi>q</mi></math></p><p>Equation <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfenced><mn>1</mn></mfenced></math>&nbsp;can be written as,</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8658;</mo><mi>p</mi><mo>&#8743;</mo><mi>q</mi><mo>&#8594;</mo><mfenced><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo>&#8744;</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow></mfenced><mo>&#8743;</mo><mfenced><mrow><mfenced><mrow><mo>~</mo><mi>p</mi><mo>&#8744;</mo><mo>~</mo><mi>r</mi></mrow></mfenced><mo>&#8744;</mo><mi>q</mi><mo>)</mo></mrow></mfenced></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8658;</mo><mo>~</mo><mfenced><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>&#8743;</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow></mfenced><mo>&#8744;</mo><mfenced><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo>&#8744;</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow></mfenced><mo>&#8743;</mo><mfenced><mrow><mfenced><mrow><mo>~</mo><mi>p</mi><mo>&#8744;</mo><mo>~</mo><mi>r</mi></mrow></mfenced><mo>&#8744;</mo><mi>q</mi><mo>)</mo></mrow></mfenced></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8658;</mo><mfenced><mrow><mo>~</mo><mi>p</mi><mo>&#8744;</mo><mo>~</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow></mfenced><mo>&#8744;</mo><mfenced><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo>&#8744;</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow></mfenced><mo>&#8743;</mo><mfenced><mrow><mfenced><mrow><mo>~</mo><mi>p</mi><mo>&#8744;</mo><mo>~</mo><mi>r</mi></mrow></mfenced><mo>&#8744;</mo><mi>q</mi><mo>)</mo></mrow></mfenced></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8658;</mo><mo>(</mo><mo>~</mo><mi>p</mi><mo>&#8744;</mo><mfenced><mrow><mo>~</mo><mi>q</mi><mo>&#8744;</mo><mi>r</mi><mo>&#8744;</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow></mfenced><mo>&#8743;</mo><mfenced><mrow><mfenced><mrow><mo>~</mo><mi>p</mi><mo>&#8744;</mo><mo>~</mo><mi>r</mi></mrow></mfenced><mo>&#8744;</mo><mi>q</mi><mo>)</mo></mrow></mfenced></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8658;</mo><mfenced><mrow><mo>~</mo><mi>p</mi><mo>&#8744;</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></mfenced><mo>&#8743;</mo><mfenced><mrow><mfenced><mrow><mo>~</mo><mi>p</mi><mo>&#8744;</mo><mo>~</mo><mi>r</mi></mrow></mfenced><mo>&#8744;</mo><mi>q</mi><mo>)</mo></mrow></mfenced></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8658;</mo><mo>~</mo><mi>p</mi><mo>&#8744;</mo><mo>~</mo><mi>r</mi><mo>&#8744;</mo><mi>q</mi></math></p><p>For above statement to be a tautology,</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>r</mi></math>&nbsp;can be&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>~</mo><mi>p</mi></math>&nbsp;or&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>q</mi></math></p><p>When <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>r</mi><mo>=</mo><mo>~</mo><mi>p</mi></math> or <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>r</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>q</mi><mo>&#8658;</mo><mo>~</mo><mi>p</mi><mo>&#8744;</mo><mo>~</mo><mi>r</mi><mo>&#8744;</mo><mi>q</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>t</mi></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8756;</mo></math>&nbsp;Two value of&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>r</mi></math>&nbsp;are possible</p>",
